<https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.18369720> a dcat:Dataset, crmdig:D1_Digital_Object, crm:E73_Information_Object, fdo:3DDataFDO ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy <urn:fdo-squirrel:activity/build> ;
    dct:description "3D model of the ogham stone CHUIS/1 (OG(H)AM I-KER-136; CISP CHUIS/1), a cross slab from Church Island (Oileán an Teampaill), Co. Kerry, now in the Cork Public Museum (inventory number 1777.1023, G1094). The slab measures 1.49 x 0.36 x 0.10 m and is fractured at its base. Its ogham inscription, read along the arris as BECCDINN MACI RIVVOESS, is in Primitive Irish, and a compass-drawn, incised ringed cross of Maltese type was added later; the excavator dates this design to 650-750 AD. The stone was found in a secondary position in the south-western quadrant of the island. The model was made with KIRI Engine from 77 photographs taken with a smartphone." ;
    dct:creator <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3246-3531> ;
    dct:license <http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/> ;
    dct:publisher <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q73901970> ;
    dct:title "Church Island Ogham Stone CHUIS/1 (Cork Public Museum)" ;
