    fdo:context "Found at Church Island (Oileán an Teampaill), Co. Kerry (SMR KE079-032004-), in a secondary position in the south-western quadrant of the island; now displayed in the Cork Public Museum, Cork (51.896085, -8.494222), inventory number 1777.1023 (G1094). Findspot and present location are different places; the spatial point of this FDO is the findspot. Described in OG(H)AM entry I-KER-136; CISP CHUIS/1; no CIIC number is listed." ;
    dct:type <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q2016147> ;
    dct:subject <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q106675412> ;
    dct:subject <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q22731> ;
    fdo:documentationPurpose "Photogrammetric documentation of an ogham stone in a museum collection (Ogham in 3D, Cork 3D)." ;
    fdo:overallCondition "Good; fractured at its base." ;
    fdo:conservationUrgency "low" ;
    fdo:acquisitionMethod "Photogrammetry (structure from motion) with KIRI Engine" ;
    fdo:acquisitionHardware "Samsung Galaxy S22" ;
    fdo:acquisitionImagesCount "77" ;
    dct:provenance "KIRI Engine (photo alignment, dense cloud, mesh, texture, export); Sketchfab upload: 1,711,370 faces, 856,009 vertices. For this FDO the model was re-oriented in Blender (180 degrees about the vertical axis, Euler XYZ 0,0,180) so that the preview shows the front instead of the back; the Sketchfab original is unchanged."  .

